On Mon, Jul 21, 2008 at 07:54, Mateusz Grotek <unoduetre@poczta.onet.pl> wrote:
> Thank you for clarification.
> I have also some question not exactly about lojban, but tried to find help
> elsewhere and couldn't. I know that lojban have context-free grammar. Is it
> possible to create analytic grammar (PEG for example) directly from
> context-free grammar? And is it possible to create fast parser from context
> free grammar. I'm completely new in parsing. Could you give me some books
> titles concerning these issues (best will be pdf's).
> Thank you very much.

I am in the process of writing a parser based on the PEG grammar and
morphology with very flexible output formats and soon to be very fast
(for PEGs anyway) parsing using Rats! generated parsers. So if you
have a need for such a parser, there's no reason to duplicate too much
work, unless its being written in C# is a dealbreaker.

